= Introduction
// Thesis: grown, not configured; as few hand-designed modules as possible.
// Ricœur: idem (sameness of substance) vs ipse (selfhood kept through time). We target ipse.
// The claim of emergence is a debt: the self-probe must be instrumented from the start.
// Why now: the scaffold makes every organ pure, so the robot's whole life is a dataset.

Contributions:
+ *A developmental scaffold.* Typed bus, pure step organs, one body interface;
  the same brain runs live, from tape, in simulation and in sleep, on a K1 and a G1.
+ *Interoception as observation* and prediction error as the shared signal, with
  global precision (arousal, fatigue, curiosity) in place of scattered thresholds.
+ *A self-probe from day one* (E0), after @emergent_self, tracked across months.
+ *Three pre-registered supporting experiments* (E1–E3) and a lesion study.
+ *An open release:* bus, step runtime, tapes, organ-swap benchmark.
